    "multi_column_eEEejx": {
      "type": "multi-column",
      "blocks": {
        "column_46tWVB": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/measure.jpg",
            "media_scale": 100,
            "heading": "Find your custom fit",
            "text": "<p>Begin by taking a measurement of your nipple size (diameter) and comparing it to <a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/cdn/shop/files/Ameda_Flange_Size_Guide.pdf?v=8656739755394763194\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.ameda.com/cdn/shop/files/Ameda_Flange_Size_Guide.pdf?v=8656739755394763194\">Ameda’s flange sizing chart</a>. Remember, your nipple should move freely within the flange tunnel without rubbing against the sides. If your breast tissue or areola is pulled in, or your nipples are stretched uncomfortably, the flange may be too large.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_YwUGqD": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/guidance.jpg",
            "media_scale": 100,
            "heading": "Seek Professional Guidance",
            "text": "<p>If you’re unsure about your fit, working with a lactation consultant can help you identify the size and style specifically designed for your needs. This is especially helpful for new moms who are still adjusting after pregnancy. For help finding a lactation consultant, visit our <a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/pages/lactation-support\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">lactation support page</span></a>.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "column_46tWVB",
        "column_YwUGqD"
      ],
