    "faq_D7XQMe": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_z4yEFm": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "What Happens If My Flange Doesn’t Fit Correctly?",
            "text": "<p>If your flange doesn't fit correctly, it can cause discomfort and reduced milk flow. To check the fit, observe your nipple during pumping:</p><ul><li><strong>Good Fit:</strong> Your nipple moves freely, and you see space around it with minimal areola drawn into the flange tunnel.</li><li><strong>Too Small:</strong> Your nipple rubs against the sides of the flange tunnel.</li><li><strong>Too Large:</strong> More of your areola is drawn into the tunnel, and your areola may rub against the flange.</li></ul><p>If your flange is too small or too large, try a different size.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_RqnkCj": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Can I Use Ameda Flanges with Other Pumps?",
            "text": "<p>Ameda flanges are designed specifically for use with Ameda breast pumps. Soft Flange Inserts are compatible only with Ameda standard 24mm flanges.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_PjjkWj": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Are Soft Inserts Necessary?",
            "text": "<p>Soft inserts are not required but are a great option for moms who experience nipple discomfort or friction during pumping. These inserts come in a wide range of sizes from 11mm to 21mm, offering flexibility for a more customized and comfortable fit. They help minimize discomfort while maintaining suction strength.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_7RQk6w": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Why Choose Ameda for Breast Pump Flanges?",
            "text": "<p>Ameda breast pump flanges are designed for comfort, durability, and a customizable fit. With a variety of sizes and options, we ensure that you can find the right fit for better milk flow and a more comfortable pumping experience.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "question_7gF6zq": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "What Are Some Breast Pump Care and Maintenance Tips? ",
            "text": "<p>To ensure your Ameda breast pump flanges stay in good condition:</p><ul><li>Clean before first use and after each use by washing in warm, soapy water or by placing them on the top rack of the dishwasher (following product guidelines).</li><li>Inspect for cracks or chips, as this can affect performance—if damaged, contact Ameda for replacements.</li><li>Store on a clean surface to avoid contamination.</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
