    "media_with_text_fHBbiQ": {
      "type": "media-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_jzXwU7": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "A Learning Curve for Moms",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "heading_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_REdFVY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Finding the right flange fit can feel overwhelming, especially for new moms navigating the early stages of breastfeeding. Breasts are still adjusting to milk production, and even experienced moms may need to reassess their flange size and comfort as their journey progresses.</p><p>Experimenting with different flange sizes and consulting lactation experts can help you find the best fit for a more comfortable, efficient pumping experience.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
